# Third-party licenses

The `eml` binary includes the third-party Rust crates listed below. eml itself is
distributed under the MIT License (`LICENSE.txt`); each crate here is distributed
under its own license, whose full text follows.

The list covers the crates `eml_cli` depends on with its default features, on
x86_64 and aarch64 Linux, aarch64 macOS and x86_64 Windows. Development and build
dependencies are left out. Procedural macros and their dependencies run only at
compile time but remain in the list. Where a crate offers a choice of licenses,
the license text given is the one under which eml uses the crate. A crate that
ships no license file of its own is given the standard text of its license.

This file is generated by cargo-about from `about.toml` and `about.hbs`.
Do not edit it by hand; regenerate it with `nix develop -c nix/third-party-licenses.sh`.

